/-!
# Specs: certificates, hostname matching, CertificateVerify

* A real chain (example.com, captured 2026-11-19 with `openssl s_client`) and the system root it
  chains to, validated at a fixed time; then the same chain with a wrong host, after expiry,
  and with one flipped signature bit.
* The RFC 8448 server certificate and its CertificateVerify (RSA-PSS-SHA256).
* RFC 6125 hostname cases and the P-256 key agreement.

General properties are proved in `LeanTLS.X509` (`matchLabels_wild_one`,
`matchLabels_wild_not_parent`, `matchLabels_wild_tld`) and `LeanTLS.ASN1` (`tlv_bounds`).
All examples here use `native_decide` (trusts Lean's compiler).
-/
namespace LeanTLS.Spec.X509Specs
open LeanTLS LeanTLS.X509

